cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use cma in academic, applied, or compliance work, please
  cite it using the metadata below. The MCP distribution wrapper
  (cma-mcp, in this repository under cma-mcp/) is a separately
  citeable artifact; see the references block.
title: "cma: notes you write, shown again on a later edit"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lucic
    given-names: Lovro
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-9976-6933"
repository-code: "https://github.com/lluvr/cma"
url: "https://github.com/lluvr/cma"
abstract: >-
  cma stores notes you choose to write and can show a matching note
  on a later edit. A file name is matched first, then auth, payments,
  or db. The counts are notes you recorded. Whether a note changes
  the next failure is unmeasured. Action-time display ships for
  Claude Code (PreToolUse and SessionStart hooks) and shell
  environments (zsh native preexec, bash via bash-preexec). cma is
  methodology-agnostic at the substrate level; vocabulary lives in
  the methodology, not in cma.
keywords:
  - compound-practice
  - failure-capture
  - decision-tracking
  - prevention
license: Apache-2.0
version: "1.2.0"
date-released: "2026-11-24"
references:
  - type: software
    title: "cma-mcp: MCP server for the cma command on PATH"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lucic
        given-names: Lovro
        orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-9976-6933"
    url: "https://github.com/lluvr/cma/tree/main/cma-mcp"
    license: Apache-2.0
    notes: >-
      Lives in this repository under cma-mcp/. Runs the cma command
      for MCP-compatible AI clients (Claude Desktop, Cursor, Cline,
      Continue.dev). The result matches the cma binary on PATH.
      See cma-mcp/CITATION.cff for its citable form.
